203a-4725).\n\n`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py` is AT the 800 LOC hard cap enforced by the CI module-size\ngate (limit single-sourced in .github/module-size-limit.txt, and locked — a normal contributor\nchange to the limit fails CI). Promoting the `llm` package into the mypy tier-1 ratchet requires\nadding annotations to this file, and any net-additive edit to a file already at the cap fails the\ngate. The split must therefore land BEFORE the llm typing story, not alongside it.\n\n## Approach\nSplit ONLY along a call-graph seam that already exists — extract a cluster of functions that\nalready call each other. Per AGENTS.md: never split mechanically to hit a number, and never create\nfiles < 100 LOC by splitting. Target 200-500 LOC per resulting file.\n\nThis is a behaviour-preserving refactor. It must not change plan-review verdicts.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py` is under the 800 LOC cap with real headroom (not one or\n      two lines), and no new file is under 100 LOC.\n- [ ] The module-size gate passes without touching .github/module-size-limit.txt.\n- [ ] The split follows an existing call-graph seam; the commit message names the seam.\n- [ ] Plan-review behaviour is unchanged: existing plan-review tests pass UNMODIFIED.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass; the complexity ratchet shows no new or increased entries.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","003c-2dd2-203a-4725"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"ffbb-9c27-78ac-489b","ticket_type":"story","title":"Split llm/plan_review/pass1.py (at the 800 LOC cap) along an existing call-graph seam","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["df87a491-ba7d-403b-81a0-854ae907